N0REP0
### :: Test case for issue #7143: opam pin edit on a package that is not pinned
### :: yet should keep the checksum of its url
### OPAMYES=1
### opam switch create pin-edit-checksum --empty
### <pkg:foo.1>
opam-version: "2.0"
url {
  src: "https://example.com/foo-1.tgz"
  checksum: "md5=d41d8cd98f00b204e9800998ecf8427e"
}
### OPAMEDITOR=cat opam pin edit foo --no-action
Package foo is not pinned. Edit as a new pinning to version 1? [Y/n] y
opam-version: "2.0"
url {
  src: "https://example.com/foo-1.tgz"
}
name: "foo"
version: "1"
[WARNING] The opam file didn't pass validation:
             error 23: Missing field 'maintainer'
           warning 25: Missing field 'authors'
           warning 35: Missing field 'homepage'
           warning 36: Missing field 'bug-reports'
           warning 37: Missing field 'dev-repo'
             error 57: Synopsis must not be empty
           warning 59: url doesn't contain a checksum
           warning 68: Missing field 'license'
Proceed anyway ('no' will re-edit)? [Y/n] y
You can edit this file again with "opam pin edit foo", export it with "opam show foo --raw"
foo is now pinned to https://example.com/foo-1.tgz (version 1)
### opam show --raw foo
opam-version: "2.0"
name: "foo"
version: "1"
url {
  src: "https://example.com/foo-1.tgz"
}
